###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0001392
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0001392> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0000000> ;
                                                   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Plant products of low molecular weight formed primarily from oxidative coupling of two p-propylphenol moieties. They can also be described as micromolecules with two phenylpropanoid units coupled together. They can be attached in various manners, like C5-C5', C8-C8'. Most known natural lignans are oxidized at C9 and C9´ and, based upon the way in which oxygen is incorporated into the skeleton and on the cyclization patterns, a wide range of lignans of very different structural types can be formed." ;
                                                   <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasBroadSynonym> "A polyphenol" ,
                                                                                                                  "Lignans" ,
                                                                                                                  "Polyphenols" ;
                                                   <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "DOI:10.1023/B:PHYT.0000045487.02836.32" ,
