###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0002661
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0002661> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0000279> ;
                                                   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Alkaloids derived from phenethylisoquinoline precursors by direct intramolecular oxidative coupling. They incorporate a nucleus A and are always pentaoxygenated at C- 1, -2, - 10, - 11, and - 12. The nitrogen function in ring B is usually N-methylated, but it may also be secondary." ;
