###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0003754
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0003754> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0000279> ;
                                                   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A small group of alkaloids typified by Akagerine, a tetracyclic compound that consist of a b-carboline fused to an azepine ring, which is substituted by a methyl group and a 2-methyl butane group. Akageran and related alkaloids appears to be formed by bond-breaking of a corynanthe precursor followed by formation of a 7-membered ring." ;
