###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0003918
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0003918> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEMONTID_0000012> ;
                                                   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Compounds in which fatty acids are linked directly to a sugar backbone, forming structures that are compatible with membrane bilayers. In the saccharolipids, a sugar substitutes for the glycerol backbone that is present in glycerolipids and glycerophospholipids. The most familiar saccharolipids contain an acylated glucosamine. In contrast to others glycolipids, the fatty acid is not glycosidically linked to the sugar moiety." ;
                                                   <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#created_by> "yandj" ;
                                                   <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#creation_date> "2014-07-21T13:26:02Z" ;
